cat > analyst-out.txt <<'EOF'
STEP 1 — DELTA
[CHANGED] api.live.app.obi.de: Envoy edge blanket-enforces 401 on the ENTIRE /v1/* tree (login, refresh, token, products, categories, search, config, healthz, .well-known/openid-configuration, swagger, docs all return 401). Route existence is not differentiable by status code; the mobile API enumeration angle is effectively closed — no unauthenticated leakage.
[CHANGED] api.obi.com: MuleSoft Anypoint Exchange partner portal reconfirmed live (200, 486KB, 14+ partner API names: order-service/inventory/product/price/transactions/subscription/seller-payout). But individual doc paths (order-service-management-api) return 404 to curl — content is SPA/client-rendered via cdn-prod-eu.anypoint.mulesoft.com. RAML/spec payloads NOT passively extractable.
[CHANGED] assets.obi.de: seller-side-panel bundle index-BUGS3Fny.js stays 404 (rotated); no replacement filename discoverable from portal HTML.

STEP 2 — PRIORITIZE
[PRIO] api.obi.com,8.2,attack_surface=10(14+ marketplace APIs),business_value=8(partner API docs only, public by design),tech_exposure=8(MuleSoft/CORS:*),gate_ease=10(public portal),cloud_surface=7(CF+nnginx→Exchange CDN),freshness=8(reconfirmed live)
[PRIO] www.obi.de,8.0,attack_surface=9(multi-API/SPA),business_value=10(e-com/10M users/payment),tech_exposure=8(Vtex/DiscoverCMS/JWT),gate_ease=6(needs browser+session),cloud_surface=8(CF+Baqend),freshness=7(stable)
[PRIO] api.live.app.obi.de,6.0,attack_surface=6(mobile API all auth-gated),business_value=9(customer data),tech_exposure=6(Envoy, no anon surface),gate_ease=2(blanket 401, needs creds),cloud_surface=6(Envoy),freshness=6(now confirmed closed)

STEP 3 — HYPOTHESES
[HYP] MuleSoft Partner Portal & Marketplace API Backend Exposure
class: MISCONFIG
asset: api.obi.com
confidence: 50
reasoning: Partner portal (Anypoint Exchange re-hosted at api.obi.com) is publicly reachable with 14+ OBI marketplace API docs named and Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *. The names are public-recon data only; the actual RAML/endpoint/schema content is SPA-rendered and not currently extractable without a browser. All order-service/product/price/inventory/transactions/seller endpoints are backend APIs that the docs describe but that are not callable from api.obi.com itself.
evidence_needed: Obtain the underlying Exchange asset GUID+version (via browser console) and fetch the published OAS/RAML for order-service-management-api to see if it exposes backend hostnames, auth token formats, or internal endpoints beyond the published partner contract.
verify_steps: (browser) load https://api.obi.com/e9d97593-.../order-service-management-api/ and read the Exchange asset version from the portal API response, then GET the published spec and diff against public docs for internal-only reveals.
impact: If docs reveal internal-only endpoints or secrets, attackers gain material recon for targeting marketplace/order APIs. Standalone, public partner docs = LOW (recon only, by-design portal). Severity: LOW-MEDIUM.
testability: HUMAN_ONLY (SPA; RAML not curl-extractable)
[HYP] www.obi.de JWT Validation alg Confusion
class: AUTH
asset: www.obi.de/account/api/public/jwt/validate
confidence: 60
reasoning: Endpoint path confirmed present in production JS. All /api/* return 404 to curl at CloudFront because origin routing requires browser UA + session cookies; the endpoint is only reachable in a real browser session. If it validates JWTs and accepts alg:none or RS256→HS256 key confusion, attacker who obtains any customer JWT (e.g., via open redirect/other flaw) could forge tokens for ATO of 10M+ heyOBI users.
evidence_needed: In a browser-authenticated session, capture the request the SPA makes to /account/api/public/jwt/validate, then POST a malformed/alg:none/invalid-signature JWT and observe whether validation is bypassed (returns 200/valid).
verify_steps: (browser, test account) open an authenticated heyOBI session → intercept POST to /account/api/public/jwt/validate → replay with crafted JWTs (alg:none, and HS256 using the RS256 public key) → check if accepted.
impact: Account takeover across 10M+ customers (purchase history, addresses, payment methods). Severity: CRITICAL.
testability: AUTH_HELPED (needs authenticated session + test account per program rules)
[HYP] Envoy Edge Blanket-Auth Bypass / Route Confusion
class: AUTH
asset: api.live.app.obi.de
confidence: 40
reasoning: Envoy front-proxy returns 401 uniformly for every /v1/* path and 200 empty for /v1/. Uniformity suggests blanket auth middleware, but also means an attacker cannot differentiate real vs dead routes — potential for path-based auth bypass (e.g., /v1/../, case, trailing-slash, or /v1.2/) is not evidenced.
evidence_needed: Test whether any path-normalization bypass lets a request reach a handler without auth (e.g., /v1/%2e%2e/, /V1/, /v1/%2F, trailing dot) returning non-401 status with body.
verify_steps: GET https://api.live.app.obi.de/v1/%2e%2e/users, /V1/users, /v1//users, /v1/auth/login%00, /v1/AUTH/login — compare status against baseline 401; any non-401 with differing body indicates a bypass.
impact: If a normalization bypass exists, unauthenticated access to customer/order data. Severity: HIGH.
testability: PASSIVE

STEP 4 — SELF-CRITIQUE
[PARKED] MuleSoft Partner Portal Backend Exposure — Confidence 50. Public partner portal by design; RAML/spec not curl-extractable; value is conditional on specs revealing internal-only data which is unconfirmed. Parked pending browser-assisted asset-version extraction (HUMAN_ONLY).
[PARKED] Envoy Path-Normalization Auth Bypass — Confidence 40, borderline. Uniform 401 is consistent with correct blanket auth; probing normalization is cheap and read-only but currently below the 40 floor without any non-401 signal observed. Parked; rewind only if a non-401 path is ever observed.
[FINAL] www.obi.de JWT Validation alg Confusion — confidence 60, AUTH_HELPED. Only surviving high-value, credible, non-rejected hypothesis. Endpoint path is real in prod JS; no passive counter-evidence. Requires authenticated session + test account.

STEP 5 — NEXT ACTION
